  message: "CORRECTION TO MY OWN FILING, same day. The description says 'THE MECHANISM TO REUSE ALREADY EXISTS AND IS NOT A NEW DESIGN' and points at io_mode argument discrimination. **That is wrong, and the difference is the whole design question.**\n\nRead in source: io_mode DISCRIMINATES BETWEEN TWO BOUNDARIES when both are plausible for the same call -- fopen(path, 'r') is fs_read, fopen(path, 'w') is fs_write, and mode_discriminated_primitives()/mode_argument_for() pick which. It has no way to express 'for this literal the row does not apply AT ALL'.\n\nprocess.on needs the second thing. process.on('message', ...) is ipc_recv; process.on('uncaughtException', ...) is not a boundary of any kind. That is a ROW ACTIVATION gate, not a boundary chooser.\n\nAnd IoPrimitive has no field for it: its declarable surface is boundary, module, name, kind, notes, simultaneous, unvouched, abstains_to. None of those can say 'only when argument 0 is this literal'.\n\nSO THIS ITEM NEEDS A DESIGN DECISION IT DID NOT ADMIT TO NEEDING. The options, none chosen here:\n  (a) a new per-row property (an argument-literal allowlist), which is new catalogue surface and would want the ADR-0024 treatment;\n  (b) SPLIT THE ROW -- drop process.on and add a narrower primitive keyed on the event, if the analyzer can carry the literal into the primitive name;\n  (c) DELETE the row and declare the process-IPC surface a dated blindness, on the grounds that the two live sites measured are both error handlers and the 'message' form did not appear at all in the corpus sampled.\n\nOption (c) deserves weighing rather than dismissing: the ONLY evidence this session has is two sites, both false. A row whose only observed firings are wrong is not obviously better than no row.\n\nWHAT DOES NOT CHANGE: the defect is real and the analyzer is not at fault. WI-kikar correctly stopped treating process as external; the row over-matches."  # c85c
